  "general_period_nonemptiness_criterion": {
    "exact_criterion": "The stratum is nonempty iff a character of Q is nontrivial on every forbidden-root image. If R0 is primitive, Q is free and the criterion reduces to no forbidden root lying in R0; a generic character avoids all remaining root hypertori.",
    "independent_gate": "A nonempty period stratum only controls (-2)-roots. Equality with the Coxeter cone separately requires equality with C_D++: all effective numerical exceptional and negative boundary walls must be present or redundant.",
    "setup": "For intended root sublattice R0 in Lambda, put Q=Lambda/R0 and F=Phi\\R0. The exact-root stratum consists of characters chi in Hom(Q,C*) with chi(beta_bar)!=1 for every beta in F.",
    "worked_case": "R0=Z.A is primitive in Lambda=A2(-1), Q=Z.delta, and the two forbidden root pairs have nonzero image +/-delta, so t!=1 is nonempty."
  },
